# Normalize line endings so the working tree stops churning between CRLF and
# LF. Without this, editing a file on Windows rewrites every line and the diff
# becomes unreadable. After changing anything here, run:
#   git add --renormalize .
#
# Default: treat everything as text and store/check out with LF. Git still
# auto-detects binary content and leaves it alone. Later rules override.
*             text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files must keep CRLF or cmd.exe can misparse them.
*.bat         text eol=crlf

# Binary files: never touched by the text filters.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
